From: DAW-GE-Proton contributors
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 18:30:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] d3d11: Prepare shared resources before keyed-mutex release

D3D11 rendering may remain deferred until a render pass is materialized.  In
that state WaitForResource can see no tracked GPU access and return before the
deferred write has been recorded or submitted.  ReleaseSync then publishes the
new keyed-mutex value, allowing another process to acquire the texture while it
still contains stale data.

Release the texture as an external resource before waiting for it.  This ends
pending rendering, records the required external-resource transition, and lets
the existing wait cover the resulting GPU work before the mutex value becomes
visible.  This fixes cross-process D3D11 shared textures without a device-wide
flush or application-specific handling.
---
 src/d3d11/d3d11_resource.cpp | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/src/d3d11/d3d11_resource.cpp b/src/d3d11/d3d11_resource.cpp
--- a/src/d3d11/d3d11_resource.cpp
+++ b/src/d3d11/d3d11_resource.cpp
@@ -122,6 +122,7 @@ namespace dxvk {
       if (!multithread.GetMultithreadProtected() && !std::exchange(s_errorShown, true))
         Logger::warn("D3D11DXGIKeyedMutex::ReleaseSync: Called without context locking enabled.");

+      context->Release11on12Resource(m_resource, texture->GetImage()->info().layout);
       D3D10DeviceLock lock = context->LockContext();
       context->WaitForResource(*texture->GetImage(), DxvkCsThread::SynchronizeAll, D3D11_MAP_READ_WRITE, 0);
     }
